::Q1::Which is a common LLM use case in software development? 
{
=Code generation
~Network cable installation
~Database hardware manufacturing
~Physical server assembly
}

::Q2::What can LLMs contribute to code review? 
{
~They permanently approve every change
~They guarantee architectural decisions are correct
=They can surface potential issues such as unused variables or inconsistent naming
~They replace every human reviewer
}

::Q3::What should a developer do with generated code before relying on it? 
{
=Review and verify it against the actual requirements
~Assume it is correct because it compiles
~Execute it automatically without inspection
~Publish it without testing
}

::Q4::What is one benefit of LLM assistance during code review? 
{
~It replaces version control
=It can quickly surface some categories of issues consistently
~It removes the need for design judgment
~It guarantees the absence of security vulnerabilities
}

::Q5::Which workflow best reflects responsible LLM use? 
{
~Avoid testing generated code
~Accept every suggestion automatically
~Generate and execute without review
=Generate assistance, review it, verify it, then use it where appropriate
}